A square in the [[Geography/Black and White/index|Black and White]], past the black doorway at the threshold in the [[Pharos]]. It stands in night, and the rain falls without a sound, and nothing can be felt there, living or dead.

Four buildings face the square. Save Your Soul Incorporated, boarded up and with fallen roof blocking its door, has three speakers on poles in front of it. The Soundscape Theaters, a cinema advertising a film in neon, is boarded up and has one speaker. The Horizon Gate Hotel, also boarded up, has one speaker. Vermillion Square Station is a stairway down to an underground tram station, and is the one building of the four not closed. Its name is close to that of the Vermilion Hotel in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]], though it is not the same place.

Inside Vermillion Square Station a tram stands with its front against a tunnel, and a moth about a foot across sits in the driver's cab, its wings making a sound like a piano. A voice box carried near the moth grows warm.
